<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The `Zzz` mark, drawn for a 24dp tile.

  Quick Settings tints tile icons by state, so only the alpha channel survives:
  this is a silhouette by necessity, not by style. It also has to carry the
  meaning alone, because the maintainer runs the tile 1x1 and some panels show
  no label beside it.

  **Three Zs rising to the right and shrinking as they go** (maintainer,
  2026-08-12): the big one sits at the bottom left where the sleeper would be,
  and the smallest drifts off the top right. One `Z` reads as a letter; the
  climbing, shrinking trio is what reads as asleep.

  **Stroked with round caps and joins, not filled.** A filled Z is two bars and
  a hard diagonal, which at this size reads as a zigzag — closer to a lightning
  bolt than to sleep. An even-weight stroke with rounded ends reads as
  handwriting, and it costs less area than a filled wedge, which is what lets
  three glyphs fit in 24dp at all.

  **Nothing touches**, and the clearance is measured on the ink rather than on
  these coordinates: a round cap puts half a stroke past every endpoint, so the
  gaps between the three bands are sized against the strokes (1.5dp of clear
  space) rather than against the path boxes. That matters most under the tint
  that blooms — the active tile inverts (light ground when off, dark when on)
  and the system tints the glyph to contrast with whichever it drew, so the same
  asset is dark-on-light *and* light-on-dark, and only the second direction
  thickens strokes and closes gaps. `TileMarkScreenshotTest` records both at the
  tile's real size, since a mark that only survives blown up is no use here.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="?android:attr/colorControlNormal">
    <path
        android:pathData="M15.62,2.95 L19.45,2.95 L15.62,6.01 L19.45,6.01"
        android:strokeColor="@android:color/white"
        android:strokeWidth="1.3"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M10.22,8.94 L15.06,8.94 L10.22,12.81 L15.06,12.81"
        android:strokeColor="@android:color/white"
        android:strokeWidth="1.55"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M4.82,16.01 L10.78,16.01 L4.82,20.77 L10.78,20.77"
        android:strokeColor="@android:color/white"
        android:strokeWidth="1.85"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round" />
</vector>
